      "date": "1974-07-11",
      "kind": "planning decision",
      "description": "The 25-by-100-foot lot held a building of three flats whose ground floor was used by Mother Goose, Inc., a nonprofit, for offices, meetings, storage, workshop and rehearsal space; no off-street parking was provided. The City Planning Commission unanimously approved, with five conditions, a conditional use allowing Mother Goose, Inc. to keep using the ground floor for office, meeting, storage, workshop and rehearsal space.",
